<%#
  T-37 / FR-71 — THE FINDINGS PANEL, BESIDE THE EDITOR AND NOT IN A GUTTER.

  --- WHY THERE IS NO GUTTER, AND WHY THAT IS SETTLED RATHER THAN A COMPROMISE ---

  `technical-spec.md` §9b.1 originally asked for a vendored CodeMirror 6 with the findings
  marked in its gutter. `[OQ-M]` was measured on 2026-08-12 and the answer is NO: there is
  no pre-built CodeMirror 6 bundle to vendor — `codemirror@6.0.2` is a meta-package whose
  `dist/index.js` is a 4 737-byte re-export shim importing seven bare specifiers, so one
  usable file needs a bundler, which §6 forbids, and the result would be OUR artefact and
  could not pass `THIRD_PARTY.md`'s three-independent-origin byte check. The curator took
  the fallback the same day: a plain `<textarea>` plus this panel.

  So the position is spelled in words — `line:column` — because that is the only way a
  panel can point at a place in a `<textarea>`. `Finding#column` exists for this view.

  --- IT WORKS WITH JAVASCRIPT OFF BY CONSTRUCTION, NOT BY DEGRADING ---

  Linting happens on the server, on the body the request carried, and this is ERB. There is
  no enhanced version of this panel to fall back FROM, which is the difference between "it
  degrades" and "it does not depend on the browser at all".

  --- WHAT IS TRANSLATED AND WHAT IS NOT ---

  The same split `_diagnostics.html.erb` makes, for the same reason: the labels are locale
  keys, and a finding's `message` is written where the rule is — in `TemplateLinter`, which
  has no I18n and must not grow one (`layer_purity.sh` keeps Rails out of `lib/`). The
  message carries the numbers and the replacement name that make it actionable; a
  translated half-sentence with the identifier removed would be worse in every language.

  `analysis` is a `TemplateLinter::Analysis`. It is never nil: every action that renders
  the editor sets it, and a body of `nil` analyses to an empty finding list rather than to
  a missing panel.
%>
<div class="box" id="reporter-template-lint">
  <h3><%= l(:label_reporter_template_lint) %></h3>

  <% if analysis.findings.empty? %>
    <%# THE CLEAN STATE IS SAID OUT LOUD. An empty panel is indistinguishable from a panel
        that failed to run, and the author has just been told this template executes
        server-side code — "nothing found" is the sentence they are looking for. %>
    <p class="nodata" id="reporter-template-lint-clean">
      <%= l(:text_reporter_template_lint_clean) %>
    </p>
  <% else %>
    <p><%= reporter_lint_summary(analysis) %></p>

    <table class="list">
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th><%= l(:label_reporter_lint_severity) %></th>
          <th><%= l(:label_reporter_lint_position) %></th>
          <th><%= l(:label_reporter_lint_rule) %></th>
          <th><%= l(:label_reporter_lint_message) %></th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <% reporter_lint_findings(analysis).each do |finding| %>
          <tr class="reporter-lint-<%= reporter_lint_severity_class(finding) %>">
            <td><%= reporter_lint_severity_label(finding) %></td>
            <%# The position is the actionable value, so it is selectable text of its own
                rather than part of a sentence — the same treatment the diagnostics panel
                gives a correlation id. %>
            <td><code><%= finding.position %></code></td>
            <td><code><%= finding.rule %></code></td>
            <td>
              <%= finding.message %>
              <% if finding.count > 1 %>
                <em class="info"><%= l(:text_reporter_lint_repeated, count: finding.count) %></em>
              <% end %>
              <% if finding.excerpt.present? %>
                <%# The author's own line, bounded by EXCERPT_LIMIT in the linter, so a
                    minified 40 KB line cannot become the page. %>
                <div><code class="reporter-lint-excerpt"><%= finding.excerpt %></code></div>
              <% end %>
            </td>
          </tr>
        <% end %>
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <% if reporter_lint_undisplayed(analysis).positive? %>
      <%# BOUNDED, AND THE BOUND IS STATED. The counts above are complete; this list is
          not, and saying so is the difference between a bound and a lie. %>
      <p class="warning">
        <%= l(:text_reporter_template_lint_more, count: reporter_lint_undisplayed(analysis)) %>
      </p>
    <% end %>
  <% end %>

  <%# WHERE THE SAME ANSWER COMES FROM ON A SERVER. FR-71's clause is that the panel and
      the rake task are one linter, and naming the task here is how an operator finds the
      other half — `test/functional/…_lint_parity_test.rb` is what keeps the two identical. %>
  <p><em class="info"><%= l(:text_reporter_template_lint_rake) %></em></p>
</div>
